EDAT reader: the message for content without a key is one short line, "DLC skipped: no licence key supplied".

From Killzone 2 port patch 5005 (Project Pyrrhus, same author, MIT). The old four lines told the player where to put a key
file and how such a key is derived from a console licence; the game's log is attached to public issues, and the port does
not ask players for keys. The behaviour is unchanged (the file is not opened, -6).

--- a/libs/filesystem/edat.c
+++ b/libs/filesystem/edat.c
@@ -546,12 +546,8 @@
             fclose(in); return -6;
         }
         if (!have_key) {
-            fprintf(stderr,
-                "[edat] license type %u needs a RIF key and none was supplied.\n"
-                "[edat]   set PS3_RIF_KEY=<32 hex chars>, or put the 16 raw bytes in\n"
-                "[edat]   %s.rifkey -- it is derived from your own .rap for this\n"
-                "[edat]   content id, which this runtime deliberately cannot do for you.\n",
-                license, in_path);
+            /* A player sees this line for every installed DLC file: say what happened, not how a key is made. */
+            fprintf(stderr, "[edat] DLC skipped: no licence key supplied\n");
             fclose(in); return -6;
         }
     }
